</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Brazil</td>
<td>PIX, Boleto, Credit Card Installments</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Mexico</td>
<td>OXXO, SPEI, Credit Cards</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Indonesia</td>
<td>GoPay, OVO, ATM Transfers</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Vietnam</td>
<td>MoMo, ZaloPay, Bank Cards</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>Mistake 3: Applying Southeast Asian Aesthetics to LATAM Creatives</h2>
<p><strong>Problem Identification</strong>: The same creative style achieved 3.2% CTR in Vietnam but only 0.6% in Colombia. Color saturation, skin tone representation, and expression of humor all vary culturally.</p>
<p><strong>Actions Taken</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>Increase warm tones and authentic lifestyle scenes in LATAM creatives</li>
<li>Focus on product demos and discount highlights in Southeast Asian creatives</li>
<li>Build a market-specific A/B test library; validate with small budgets for 3 days before scaling</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Localization Checklist (Ready to Use)</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Language Layer</strong>: Native proofreading, holiday-sensitive word filtering, dialect adaptation (e.g., LATAM Spanish vs. Spain Spanish vocabulary differences)</li>
<li><strong>Payment Layer</strong>: Integrate top-3 local payment methods; avoid relying solely on Western payment options</li>
<li><strong>Visual Layer</strong>: Skin tone representation, color preferences, mascot/character cultural fit</li>
<li><strong>Compliance Layer</strong>: Data privacy laws (GDPR, LGPD for Brazil, PDPA for Thailand)</li>
<li><strong>Channel Layer</strong>: Prioritize TikTok and Facebook in Southeast Asia; run Google and Meta simultaneously in LATAM</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>Final Take</h2>
<p>Localization is a cost center in international ad campaigns—not an optional add-on. Every cultural misstep directly translates to wasted CPM and funnel leakage. Before entering a new market, spend two weeks on a localization audit before launching paid campaigns.</p>
